// Refined-lattice (fjc>1) MOMENT regression (ref 21 Aug 2026, synced from
// the dev tree's 20 Aug fix): the four excess-profile moment columns
// (1st_M_phi_z, 2nd_M_phi_z, RMS, fluctuations) on a spherical
// FJC_choices 5 (fjc = 2) grafted-brush layer. Guards the fix of a double
// division by fjc in Lattice1D.moment (collaborator bug report): z_phys
// is in bond units and L is the layer volume, so the L-weighted sum is
// already the refinement-consistent moment -- the extra /fjc copied from
// Namics' LGrad1::Moment in the 5 Jul 2026 physics review made every
// fjc>1 moment fjc times too small (the review matched the inner /fjc
// but missed that Namics' 1st_M caller multiplies fjc back,
// segment.cpp:1837). The molecule is PINNED (phibulk = 0) ON PURPOSE:
// theta_exc == theta, so the moments are the honest L-measure integrals
// -- with a nonzero phibulk on a CURVED fjc>1 lattice, theta_exc
// subtracts phibulk*volume with the geometric volume (4 pi R^3/3) while
// theta integrates the refined shells (sum L differs by ~3% at fjc = 2),
// and that measure mismatch pollutes the excess columns in BOTH engines
// (Namics does the same; open issue, under investigation in the dev
// tree). SELF-VALIDATING at creation: all four kal columns ==
// sum(z^n phi L)/theta recomputed from the committed .pro at machine
// precision, and fjc-CONSISTENT (<z> = 6.176/5.806/5.742 at fjc 1/2/3,
// converging under refinement, where the bug gave exactly <z>/fjc).
// ORACLE (compiled Namics, this input): theta_exc exact, 1st_M at 2e-10
// (Namics' 1st_M caller compensates its inner /fjc);
// 2nd_M/RMS/fluctuations INTENTIONALLY deviate at fjc>1 -- PySFBox
// 2nd_M = exactly fjc x Namics', whose 2nd-moment caller misses the *fjc
// compensation (reported to the Namics authors; at fjc = 2 Namics'
// M2 - M1^2 even goes negative and it prints fluctuations = 0), so the
// binary is no oracle for those three columns. fjc = 1 moments are
// bit-identical to before the fix; those columns are guarded by
// brush_in_good_solvent.in and friends. (The dev tree's twin regression
// is planar, planar_fjc_moments.in; planar fjc>1 is not in this package.)
lat : NN : n_layers : 25
lat : NN : geometry : spherical
lat : NN : lattice_type : hexagonal
lat : NN : FJC_choices : 5

mon : S : freedom : frozen
mon : S : frozen_range : 1;3
mon : P : freedom : pinned
mon : P : pinned_range : 4;4
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : W : freedom : free

mol : pol : composition : (P)1(A)24
mol : pol : freedom : restricted
mol : pol : theta : 20

mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-8

output : kal : append : false
kal : mon : A : theta_exc
kal : mon : A : 1st_M_phi_z
kal : mon : A : 2nd_M_phi_z
kal : mon : A : RMS
kal : mon : A : fluctuations

output : pro : append : false
pro : mon : A : phi

start
